Map VFIO sparse mmap areas even when the BAR holds the MSI-X tables.

Cloud Hypervisor refuses to mmap any BAR that contains the MSI-X vector
table or PBA unless the kernel advertises MSIX_MAPPABLE, and traps every
access instead. NVIDIA's vGPU vendor driver places the tables in BAR0,
does not advertise MSIX_MAPPABLE, and publishes a sparse mmap list that
already skips the vector table page. It then rejects trapped reads of
the listed bytes with EFAULT ("map-only region access"), so the guest
driver saw 0xffffffff from every register.

Accept a sparse mmap list as sufficient, like QEMU does. The areas are
mapped exactly as published: the driver returns EINVAL for a mapping
that does not match one of its areas, so they cannot be clipped.

--- a/pci/src/vfio.rs
+++ b/pci/src/vfio.rs
@@ -1774,10 +1774,16 @@
 
                 // Don't try to mmap the region if it contains MSI-X table or
                 // MSI-X PBA subregion, and if we couldn't find MSIX_MAPPABLE
-                // in the list of supported capabilities.
+                // in the list of supported capabilities. A sparse mmap list
+                // is as good: the driver already left the tables out of it,
+                // and it rejects any mapping that is not one of its areas
+                // exactly, so the list is used as published.
                 if let Some(msix) = self.common.interrupt.msix.as_ref()
                     && (region.index == msix.cap.table_bir() || region.index == msix.cap.pba_bir())
                     && !caps.contains(&VfioRegionInfoCap::MsixMappable)
+                    && !caps
+                        .iter()
+                        .any(|c| matches!(c, VfioRegionInfoCap::SparseMmap(_)))
                 {
                     continue;
                 }
